{"title":"American Regions Mathematics League","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>American Regions Math League</b> (ARML) is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematical_problem_solving\" title=\"Mathematical problem solving\">mathematical problem solving</a> competition primarily for U.S. high school students.\n</p>\n<table style=\"border:thin solid black;padding:10px;float:right;margin:10px;background:#fff;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"border:thin solid gray;text-align:center;background:#ccf;\"><b>ARML</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Region</b>: USA\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Type</b>: Free Response\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_Wiki:Competition_ratings\" title=\"AoPS Wiki:Competition ratings\">Difficulty</a></b>: 3.5-6\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Difficulty Breakdown:</b>\n<p><u>Individual</u>: 2 (Problem 1), 3 (Problem 2/3/4), 3.5 (Problem 5/7/9), 4.5 (Problem 6/8), 6.5 (Problem 10)<br /><u>Team</u>: 3.5 (Problem 1-5), 5 (Problem 6-10)\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#How_to_participate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">How to participate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Format\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Format</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Books\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Books</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"How_to_participate\">How to participate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_Regions_Mathematics_League&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: How to participate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find out if your area has a team already.  Contact ARML for details.  If your area does not already have a team, ask ARML how to start one.\n</p><p>See the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=How_to_join_an_ARML_team\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"How to join an ARML team\">How to join an ARML team</a> wiki page for more info. Teams have 15 students. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_Regions_Mathematics_League&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: History\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>ARML was started in 1976 as a mathematics competition\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Format\">Format</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_Regions_Mathematics_League&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Format\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ARML has several different events:\n</p>\n<ul><li>A team round, in which the entire team works on ten problems together</li>\n<li>A power round, where the questions are proof-oriented and are in a theme</li>\n<li>An individual round, where each individual takes a ten question test</li>\n<li>Two relay rounds, where the answer to one problem is necessary to solve the next problem</li>\n<li>A super relay, a relay round where each team submits one answer</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_Regions_Mathematics_League&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.arml3.com\">ARML Homepage</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/community/c124_arml\">ARML Forum</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Books\">Books</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_Regions_Mathematics_League&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Books\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There are seven books of past ARML problems, one of them is hard to find, but the others are available online.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0962640166/artofproblems-20\">ARML-NYSML 1989-1994</a> (see <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=NYSML\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"NYSML\">NYSML</a>).</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://arml3.com/arml-books/\">The ARML book website</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_Regions_Mathematics_League&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ARML_historical_results\" title=\"ARML historical results\">ARML historical results</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ARML_teams\" title=\"ARML teams\">ARML teams</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_contest_books\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Math contest books\">Math contest books</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_books\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Math books\">Math books</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_ARML\" title=\"Mock ARML\">Mock ARML</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018035012\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.028 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 40/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 484/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 186/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.320      1 Template:Contest_Info\n100.00%    5.320      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1538:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018035012 and revision id 284197. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}